{
  "name": "Armor Model",
  "type": "feat",
  "_id": "4TLmfS5GwraJAxqD",
  "img": "icons/equipment/head/helm-barbute-rounded-gold.webp",
  "folder": "nToP5r4nIXNeP27o",
  "sort": 300000,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You can customize your Arcane Armor by choosing one of the following models: Dreadnaught, Guardian, or Infiltrator. The model gives you special benefits while you wear it. Each model includes a special weapon: when you attack with it, you can add your Intelligence modifier, instead of your Strength or Dexterity modifier, to the attack and damage rolls. You can change the model whenever you finish a Short or Long Rest with Smith's Tools in hand.</p><h4>Dreadnaught</h4><p>Your armor becomes a towering juggernaut in battle.</p><p><strong>Force Demolisher.</strong> An arcane wrecking ball or sledgehammer projects from your armor. It counts as a Simple Melee weapon with the Reach property and deals 1d10 Force damage on a hit. If you hit a creature at least one size smaller than you with it, you can push that creature up to 10 feet straight away from you or pull it up to 10 feet toward you.</p><p><strong>Giant Stature.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you transform and enlarge your armor for 1 minute. For the duration, your reach increases by 5 feet, and if you are smaller than Large, you become Large, along with everything you're wearing (if there isn't room, your size doesn't change). You can use this Bonus Action a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><h4>Guardian</h4><p>Your armor is designed for the front line.</p><p><strong>Thunder Pulse.</strong> You can discharge concussive blasts with strikes from your armor. The pulse counts as a Simple Melee weapon and deals 1d8 Thunder damage on a hit. A creature hit by it has Disadvantage on attack rolls against targets other than you until the start of your next turn.</p><p><strong>Defensive Field.</strong> While Bloodied, you can take a Bonus Action to gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your Artificer level. You lose them if you doff the armor.</p><h4>Infiltrator</h4><p>Your armor is made for subtler undertakings.</p><p><strong>Lightning Launcher.</strong> A gemlike node appears on your armor and shoots bolts of lightning. It counts as a Simple Ranged weapon with a normal range of 90 feet and a long range of 300 feet, and it deals 1d6 Lightning damage on a hit. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with it, you can deal an extra 1d6 Lightning damage to that target.</p><p><strong>Powered Steps.</strong> Your Speed increases by 5 feet.</p><p><strong>Dampening Field.</strong> You have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. If the armor imposes Disadvantage on such checks, the Advantage and Disadvantage cancel out.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-wFSE9YUaVHu79ugi\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Use the activities of your model. Turn on the <em>Infiltrator Model</em> effect while you use that model. The weapon damage dice increase at level 15 (see Perfected Armor): change them in the dialog.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
